IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nla-dates`

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT) -- the rules a person bringing (or answering) a claim meets: Part I (ss 4, 5, 5A, 8, 9(2)),
-- Part II so far as it fixes the periods for personal injury, other torts, contracts, deeds, money recoverable under an
-- enactment, Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 claims, defamation and contribution (ss 11, 12, 14, 17, 24), Part III
-- (postponement of the bar: disability, notices to proceed, confirmation, fraud and mistake, the court's general power to
-- extend, and the defamation extensions, ss 36-44C), s 48A, and Part V Division 2 (child abuse transitional, ss 53-55).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in nla-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "is not maintainable",
-- "but only if", "does not apply", "may not", an "if" or "where" condition that fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not
-- answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's judgments ("satisfied", "just", "just and
-- reasonable", "reasonable diligence") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Periods are
-- counted with the day of the event excluded, so the last day of a period of years is the anniversary (forks F1, F2).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Limitation Act 1981 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is
-- owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 1981`

§§ `Days fixed by the Act and its endnotes`

-- s 2 and the endnotes' list of legislation: the Act commenced on 26 February 1982 (Gaz G8, 26 February 1982).
`the commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 26 2 1982

-- s 53(1): "commencement means the commencement of the Limitation Amendment (Child Abuse) Act 2017" -- 15 June 2017
-- (endnotes, Gaz S31).
`the child abuse commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 6 2017

-- s 48A was inserted by the Supreme Court (Rules of Procedure) Act 1987, commenced 1 November 1987 (endnotes).
`the section 48A commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 11 1987

-- s 44AA was inserted by the Defamation Legislation Amendment Act 2025, commenced 11 August 2025 (endnotes); s 56(1): it
-- applies "in relation to the publication of defamatory matter after the commencement of that section" (fork F8).
`the section 44AA commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 11 8 2025

§§ `s 4 -- person under a disability`

-- s 4(1): "person under a disability means an infant or a disabled person, or a convicted person who, after conviction,
-- is undergoing a sentence of imprisonment." "disabled person means a person who, by reason of age, disease, illness or
-- mental or physical infirmity, is incapable of managing his affairs in respect of legal proceedings." "Infant" is not
-- defined: read as under 18 (the age of majority, set outside this Act; finding 2). A "means" definition: JUST FALSE
-- when no head holds.
GIVEN `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am incapable of managing my affairs in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment after conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- I am a person under a disability` `I am under 18` `I am incapable of managing my affairs in legal proceedings` `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment after conviction` MEANS
    IF `I am under 18` OR `I am incapable of managing my affairs in legal proceedings` OR `I am serving a sentence of imprisonment after conviction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A -- child abuse: no limitation period`

-- s 5A(6): "child abuse means any of the following perpetrated against a person when the person is (or was) under 18
-- years of age: (a) sexual abuse; (b) serious physical abuse; (c) psychological abuse that arises from abuse mentioned in
-- paragraph (a) or (b)." "Sexual abuse", "serious physical abuse" and "psychological abuse" are not defined: the kind is
-- asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse`
    `other abuse or harm`

-- s 5A(1): "This section applies in relation to an action for damages for personal injury to a person arising from child
-- abuse of the person." (2): "may be brought at any time and is not subject to any limitation period under this Act."
-- (3): in tort, contract, under statute or otherwise. (4): extends to Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 causes of
-- action and those surviving for the estate. A "means" definition (JUST FALSE when the abuse is not child abuse); an
-- action that is not one for damages for personal injury is outside the section's own scope (NOTHING-kind: limited by
-- its own wording).
GIVEN `it is a claim for damages for personal injury, a death claim or an estate claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the abuse was` IS A `Kind of abuse`
      `I was under 18 when it was perpetrated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury arose from that abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5A -- no limitation period applies to my child abuse action` `it is a claim for damages for personal injury, a death claim or an estate claim` `what the abuse was` `I was under 18 when it was perpetrated` `the injury arose from that abuse` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a claim for damages for personal injury, a death claim or an estate claim`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I was under 18 when it was perpetrated` AND `the injury arose from that abuse` AND (NOT (`what the abuse was` EQUALS `other abuse or harm`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 12(2)(a), (3) -- dust disease`

-- s 12(3): "dust disease means a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum that is attributable to dust."
-- A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `it is a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is attributable to dust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(3) -- it is a dust disease` `it is a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` `it is attributable to dust` MEANS
    IF `it is a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum` AND `it is attributable to dust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part II -- the periods`

-- The kinds of action the encoding answers. Land, mortgages, trusts, accounts, judgments, penalties, arbitration awards,
-- admiralty, conversion of goods, equitable relief, arrears of income and money paid under a mistake by way of tax
-- (ss 13, 15, 16, 18-23, 25-35E) are not in the claims focus and are answered "not answered by this encoding".
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `damages for personal injury`
    `another action in tort, including breach of statutory duty`
    `an action on a contract not evidenced by a deed`
    `an action on a deed`
    `an action to recover money recoverable under an enactment`
    `a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 action for a death`
    `defamation`
    `land, a mortgage, a trust, an account, a judgment, a penalty, an arbitration award, admiralty, goods, equity or tax`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the encoding covers` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `land, a mortgage, a trust, an account, a judgment, a penalty, an arbitration award, admiralty, goods, equity or tax` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The Part II period, in years.
-- s 12(1): "(a) an action founded on contract (including quasi-contract) not being a cause of action which is evidenced
-- by a deed; (b) an action founded on tort including a cause of action founded on a breach of statutory duty; ... (d) an
-- action to recover money recoverable by virtue of an enactment, other than a penalty or forfeiture" -- "3 years from the
-- date on which the cause of action first accrues". A personal injury action is founded on tort (or contract): 3 years.
-- s 12(2)(b): defamation, "one year from the date of publication". s 14(1): deed, 12 years. s 17: Compensation (Fatal
-- Injuries) Act 1974 ss 7, 13, "3 years from the date of the death" (for that kind the day given is the day of the death).
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part II period in years for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an action on a deed` THEN 12
    WHEN `defamation` THEN 1
    WHEN `land, a mortgage, a trust, an account, a judgment, a penalty, an arbitration award, admiralty, goods, equity or tax` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 3

§§ `The facts of one claim`

-- One claim, from the seat of the person to whom the cause of action accrues.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `claim kind`                          IS A `Kind of action`
    `another Act sets the period`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim is a child abuse action`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim is from a dust disease`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim accrual day`                   IS A DATE
    `claimant birth day`                  IS A DATE
    `claimant has died`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `claimant death day`                  IS A DATE
    `other disability`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `other disability began`              IS A DATE
    `other disability has ended`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `other disability ended`              IS A DATE
    `notice to proceed served`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice to proceed day`               IS A DATE
    `fraud, concealment or mistake`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud discovered`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud discovery day`                 IS A DATE
    `confirmed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `confirmation day`                    IS A DATE
    `Public Trustee order made`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `Public Trustee order day`            IS A DATE
    `concerns notice given`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `concerns notice day`                 IS A DATE

-- What the limitation period comes to.
DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period applies`
    `the last day to commence is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `time has not yet begun to count`
    `another Act's time limit applies`
    `section 9 decides, for a cause of action that arose before 26 February 1982`
    `not answered by this encoding`

§§ `Part III Division 1 -- disability (ss 36, 38)`

-- s 36(1): "where (a) a person has a cause of action; (b) the limitation period ... has commenced to run; and (c) the
-- person is under a disability, ... (d) the running of the limitation period is suspended for the duration of the
-- disability; and (e) if, but for this paragraph, the limitation period would expire before the lapse of 3 years after
-- (i) the date on which he has, before the expiration of the limitation period, ceased to be under a disability; or (ii)
-- the date of his death, whichever is the earlier, the limitation period is extended so as to expire 3 years after the
-- earlier of those dates." (2): "whenever a person is under a disability, whether or not he is under the same or another
-- disability at any time during the limitation period." (4): "does not operate so as to extend a limitation period to
-- more than 30 years from the date when the cause of action arose."
-- s 38(2): once a notice to proceed is served on a tutor or guardian, "section 36(1) applies as though the person ceased,
-- on the date of the service of the notice, to be under a disability and does not thereafter come under that disability."
--
-- Two spells are encoded: infancy (from the start of the reckoning to the 18th birthday or an earlier death) and one other
-- (a disabled person's incapacity, or a sentence of imprisonment), which ends at the earliest of its end, a notice to
-- proceed and death. Days already suspended by infancy are not counted twice; a spell that begins after the period has
-- expired has no effect; one that has not ended suspends the period until the 30-year cap (forks F3, F4).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Part III Division 1 -- the last day counted from` `the start` `for` c MEANS
    `the later of` `the ordinary last day` `and` (`the earlier of` `after the other spell` `and` `the 30 year day`)
    WHERE
        `the ordinary last day` MEANS `the anniversary` (`the Part II period in years for` (c's `claim kind`)) `years after` `the start`
        `the 30 year day` MEANS `the anniversary` 30 `years after` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`)
        `the infancy end` MEANS
            IF c's `claimant has died` AND ((c's `claimant death day`) `is before` `the 18th birthday`)
            THEN c's `claimant death day`
            ELSE `the 18th birthday`
        `infancy suspends` MEANS `the start` `is before` `the infancy end`
        `after infancy` MEANS
            IF `infancy suspends`
            THEN `the later of` (`the date` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the infancy end`) `days after` `the ordinary last day`) `and` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the infancy end`)
            ELSE `the ordinary last day`
        `the other spell start` MEANS
            IF `infancy suspends`
            THEN `the later of` (`the later of` (c's `other disability began`) `and` `the start`) `and` `the infancy end`
            ELSE `the later of` (c's `other disability began`) `and` `the start`
        `the other spell has an end` MEANS c's `other disability has ended` OR c's `notice to proceed served` OR c's `claimant has died`
        `the other spell end` MEANS
            `the earlier of` (`the earlier of` `the end given` `and` `the notice given`) `and` `the death given`
        `the end given` MEANS
            IF c's `other disability has ended`
            THEN c's `other disability ended`
            ELSE `the far day`
        `the notice given` MEANS
            IF c's `notice to proceed served`
            THEN c's `notice to proceed day`
            ELSE `the far day`
        `the death given` MEANS
            IF c's `claimant has died`
            THEN c's `claimant death day`
            ELSE `the far day`
        `the far day` MEANS `the anniversary` 1000 `years after` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        `the other spell counts` MEANS c's `other disability` AND (NOT ((c's `other disability began`) `is after` `after infancy`))
        `after the other spell` MEANS
            IF NOT `the other spell counts`
            THEN `after infancy`
            ELSE IF NOT `the other spell has an end`
                 THEN `the 30 year day`
                 ELSE IF `the other spell end` `is after` `the other spell start`
                      THEN `the later of` (`the date` (`the days from` `the other spell start` `to` `the other spell end`) `days after` `after infancy`) `and` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the other spell end`)
                      ELSE `after infancy`

§§ `Part III Division 1 -- fraud, concealment and mistake (ss 42, 43)`

-- s 42(1): where "(a) there is a cause of action based on fraud or deceit; or (b) a cause of action or the identity of a
-- person against whom a cause of action lies is fraudulently concealed, the time which elapses after a limitation period
-- ... commences to run, and before the date on which a person having ... the cause of action first discovers, or may with
-- reasonable diligence discover, the fraud, deceit or concealment ... does not count" -- against "a person answerable for
-- fraud, deceit or concealment" (s 42(3)), not an innocent purchaser (s 42(4)). s 43(1): the same for "a cause of action
-- for relief from the consequences of a mistake", until the mistake is discovered (not against an innocent purchaser,
-- s 43(3)). ss 42(2), 43(2): whether the period would have expired before or after that date. The reckoning starts on the
-- later of accrual and discovery.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the reckoning start of` c MEANS
    IF c's `fraud, concealment or mistake` AND c's `fraud discovered`
    THEN `the later of` (c's `claim accrual day`) `and` (c's `fraud discovery day`)
    ELSE c's `claim accrual day`

§§ `Part III Division 1 -- confirmation (s 41) and the Public Trustee order (s 39(3))`

-- s 41(1): where "after a limitation period ... commences to run but before the expiration of the limitation period, a
-- person against whom ... the cause of action lies confirms the cause of action, the time during which the limitation
-- period runs before the date of the confirmation does not count". The period counts afresh from the confirmation; a
-- confirmation on the first day of the reckoning or on the last day counts (fork F5).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the confirmation counts for` c IF
    c's `confirmed`
        AND (NOT ((c's `confirmation day`) `is before` (`the reckoning start of` c)))
        AND (NOT ((c's `confirmation day`) `is after` (`Part III Division 1 -- the last day counted from` (`the reckoning start of` c) `for` c)))

-- s 39(3): after an order appointing the Public Trustee as the infant's tutor, the action "shall not be brought ... after
-- the expiration of (a) a limitation period of 3 years from the date of the order; or (b) the limitation period otherwise
-- fixed by or under this Act ..., whichever is the later."
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the Part III last day of` c MEANS
    IF c's `Public Trustee order made`
    THEN `the later of` `before the order` `and` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` (c's `Public Trustee order day`))
    ELSE `before the order`
    WHERE
        `from the reckoning` MEANS `Part III Division 1 -- the last day counted from` (`the reckoning start of` c) `for` c
        `before the order` MEANS
            IF `the confirmation counts for` c
            THEN `the later of` `from the reckoning` `and` (`Part III Division 1 -- the last day counted from` (c's `confirmation day`) `for` c)
            ELSE `from the reckoning`

§§ `Part III Division 3 -- defamation: concerns notice (s 44AA)`

-- s 44AA(1): "The 1-year limitation period referred to in section 12(2)(b) is taken to have been extended as provided by
-- subsection (2) if a concerns notice is given to the proposed defendant on a day (the notice day) within the period of 56
-- days before the limitation period expires." (2): "for an additional period of 56 days minus any days remaining after
-- the notice day until the 1-year limitation period expires." The Act's example ("given 7 days before the limitation
-- period expires ... 6 days left after the notice day ... 56 days minus 6 days, that is, 50 days") counts as "remaining"
-- only the days strictly between the notice day and the day the period expires (the last day). So a notice given 1 to 56
-- days before the last day extends the period to 57 days after the notice day, and one given on the last day to 56 days
-- after it (finding 6, fork F9). s 56(1): only for publication after 11 August 2025.
GIVEN `the last day` IS A DATE, c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 44AA -- the last day after a concerns notice` `the last day` c MEANS
    IF (c's `claim kind` EQUALS `defamation`)
            AND c's `concerns notice given`
            AND (NOT ((c's `claim accrual day`) `is before` `the section 44AA commencement day`))
            AND (`the days before` AT LEAST 0)
            AND (`the days before` AT MOST 56)
    THEN `the date` (56 MINUS `the days remaining`) `days after` `the last day`
    ELSE `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the days before` MEANS `the days from` (c's `concerns notice day`) `to` `the last day`
        `the days remaining` MEANS max 0 (`the days before` MINUS 1)

§§ `The limitation period for the claim (ss 5, 5A, 9, 11, 12, 14, 17, Part III)`

-- s 5: "This Act does not apply to any action for which a period of limitation is prescribed by any other enactment" --
-- asked as a fact. s 5A(2): child abuse, "Despite any other provision of this Act ... may be brought at any time" (and,
-- by s 5A(4), a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act claim). s 12(2)(a): "no limitation period applies to an action for
-- damages for personal injury arising from a dust disease" (a death claim is under s 17, not s 12(1): finding 4).
-- s 9(2): a cause of action that arose before 26 February 1982 expires at the later of the old law's time and this
-- Act's; the old law is not encoded. Fraud not yet discovered: the time has not begun to count (s 42).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the encoding covers` (c's `claim kind`))
        THEN `not answered by this encoding`
        IF c's `another Act sets the period`
        THEN `another Act's time limit applies`
        IF c's `claim is a child abuse action` AND ((c's `claim kind` EQUALS `damages for personal injury`) OR (c's `claim kind` EQUALS `a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 action for a death`))
        THEN `no limitation period applies`
        IF c's `claim is from a dust disease` AND (c's `claim kind` EQUALS `damages for personal injury`)
        THEN `no limitation period applies`
        IF (c's `claim accrual day`) `is before` `the commencement day`
        THEN `section 9 decides, for a cause of action that arose before 26 February 1982`
        IF c's `fraud, concealment or mistake` AND (NOT (c's `fraud discovered`))
        THEN `time has not yet begun to count`
        OTHERWISE `the last day to commence is` (`s 44AA -- the last day after a concerns notice` (`the Part III last day of` c) c)

§§ `Commencing in time -- a regulative rule (s 12 and Part II)`

-- "is not maintainable after the expiration of a limitation period" is modelled as what the plaintiff must do to keep
-- the action: MUST commence WITHIN the days from accrual to the last day, LEST the action is barred. The helper runs the
-- rule over the day of the step: on the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so
-- FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`
    `the parent or guardian`
    `the putative defendant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `commence the action`
    `bring the action as guardian ad litem`
    `apply for the Public Trustee to be appointed tutor`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the action must be commenced within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `commence the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired: the action is not maintainable unless a court extends the time (s 44, s 44A)"

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
      `the actor` IS A `Party`
      `the step` IS A `Step`
      `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step satisfies` `the rule` `by` `the actor` `doing` `the step` `at` `the time of the step` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the actor` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether the action is maintainable if commenced on a day. JUST FALSE once the period has run ("is not maintainable");
-- JUST TRUE where no period applies ("may be brought at any time") or none has begun to count; NOTHING before accrual,
-- under the old law, another Act, or outside the encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `the day of commencing` IS A DATE, c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the action can be commenced on` `the day of commencing` `for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time limit for` c
    WHEN `no limitation period applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `time has not yet begun to count` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `the day of commencing` `is before` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the action must be commenced within` (`the days from` (c's `claim accrual day`) `to` `the final day`)) `by` `the plaintiff` `doing` `commence the action` `at` (`the days from` (c's `claim accrual day`) `to` `the day of commencing`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 39 -- notice to an infant's parent or guardian: a regulative rule`

-- s 39(1): the putative defendant "may serve on a parent or guardian of an infant a notice requiring the parent or
-- guardian to bring, as guardian ad litem, within 6 months after the date of the service of the notice, an action against
-- the putative defendant". (2): if the parent or guardian "fails to comply with the notice within the time specified",
-- the putative defendant "may apply to the Supreme Court for an order appointing the Public Trustee to be the tutor of the
-- infant". The duty is modelled as MUST bring the action WITHIN the days to 6 months after service, LEST the putative
-- defendant MAY apply. Failing the notice does not bar the infant's action: s 39(3) then gives 3 years from any order.
GIVEN `the service day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 39 -- the last day under the notice` `the service day` MEANS `the date` 6 `months after` `the service day`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the parent must bring the action within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the parent or guardian`
    MUST `bring the action as guardian ad litem`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the putative defendant`
        MAY `apply for the Public Trustee to be appointed tutor`

DECLARE `Notice outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the notice was complied with`
    `the notice was not complied with: the person you would sue may ask the Supreme Court to appoint the Public Trustee as your tutor`

GIVEN `the service day` IS A DATE, `the day brought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice outcome`
`s 39 -- the outcome of the notice` `the service day` `the day brought` MEANS
    IF (`the day brought` `is before` `the service day`) OR `brought in time`
    THEN `the notice was complied with`
    ELSE `the notice was not complied with: the person you would sue may ask the Supreme Court to appoint the Public Trustee as your tutor`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed here` MEANS `the days from` `the service day` `to` (`s 39 -- the last day under the notice` `the service day`)
        `brought in time` MEANS `the step satisfies` (`the parent must bring the action within` `the days allowed here`) `by` `the parent or guardian` `doing` `bring the action as guardian ad litem` `at` (`the days from` `the service day` `to` `the day brought`)

§§ `s 41 -- confirmation`

-- s 41(2)(a): "a person confirms a cause of action if, but only if: (i) he makes in writing, and signs, an acknowledgment
-- to a person having ... the cause of action, of the right or title of the person to whom the acknowledgment is made; or
-- (ii) he makes, to a person having ... the cause of action, a payment in respect of the right or title". (4): it may be
-- relied on if made to the person "or to a person through whom he claims". (5): binds the maker or one to whom the
-- liability devolves. s 40(1)(e): a notice under s 38 or 39 "is not a confirmation". "But only if": JUST FALSE otherwise.
DECLARE `Kind of confirmation` IS ONE OF
    `a written acknowledgment of my right, signed by its maker`
    `a payment in respect of my right`
    `an acknowledgment not in writing or not signed`
    `a notice to proceed under section 38 or 39`
    `nothing of that kind`

DECLARE `Confirmation effect` IS ONE OF
    `the period counts afresh from` HAS `the confirmation day` IS A DATE
    `this is not a confirmation that binds the person I would sue`
    `too late: the limitation period had already expired`

GIVEN `what was given` IS A `Kind of confirmation`
      `it was made to me or to someone I claim through` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by the person I would sue or someone whose liability has passed to them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE
      `the accrual day` IS A DATE
      `the last day before it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Confirmation effect`
`s 41 -- what the confirmation does` `what was given` `it was made to me or to someone I claim through` `it was made by the person I would sue or someone whose liability has passed to them` `the day it was made` `the accrual day` `the last day before it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a confirmation` AND `it was made to me or to someone I claim through` AND `it was made by the person I would sue or someone whose liability has passed to them`)
        THEN `this is not a confirmation that binds the person I would sue`
        IF (`the day it was made` `is before` `the accrual day`) OR (`the day it was made` `is after` `the last day before it`)
        THEN `too late: the limitation period had already expired`
        OTHERWISE `the period counts afresh from` `the day it was made`
    WHERE
        `a confirmation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what was given`
            WHEN `a written acknowledgment of my right, signed by its maker` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a payment in respect of my right` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 44 -- the court's general power to extend`

DECLARE `Court extension` IS ONE OF
    `the court may extend the time, to the extent and on the terms it thinks fit`
    `this section gives no extension on these facts`
    `section 44 does not apply to defamation`
    `there is no limitation period to extend`

-- s 44(1): where "this or any other Act ... prescribes or limits the time for (a) instituting an action ... a court may
-- extend the time". (3): "This section does not ... (aa) apply to an action on a cause of action for defamation; or (b)
-- empower a court to extend a limitation period prescribed by this Act unless it is satisfied that: (i) facts material
-- to the plaintiff's case were not ascertained by him until some time within 12 months before the expiration of the
-- limitation period or occurring after the expiration of that period, and that the action was instituted within 12
-- months after the ascertainment of those facts by the plaintiff; or (ii) the plaintiff's failure to institute the action
-- within the limitation period resulted from representations or conduct of the defendant ... and was reasonable ...,
-- and that in all the circumstances of the case, it is just to grant the extension of time." (7): personal injury and
-- fatal injuries actions even where the period expired before the application. The (i) dates are worked out: the facts
-- learnt after the same day a year before the last day (fork F6), the action instituted no later than the anniversary of
-- that day. Materiality, (ii) and "just" are the court's.
GIVEN `it is defamation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a limitation period applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is set by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day` IS A DATE
      `material facts were learnt late` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I learnt them` IS A DATE
      `the day I instituted or will institute` IS A DATE
      `the court is satisfied the facts are material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied the delay came from the defendant and was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied it is just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`s 44 -- the court may extend` `it is defamation` `a limitation period applies` `the period is set by this Act` `the last day` `material facts were learnt late` `the day I learnt them` `the day I instituted or will institute` `the court is satisfied the facts are material` `the court is satisfied the delay came from the defendant and was reasonable` `the court is satisfied it is just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is defamation`
        THEN `section 44 does not apply to defamation`
        IF NOT `a limitation period applies`
        THEN `there is no limitation period to extend`
        IF NOT `the period is set by this Act`
        THEN `the court may extend the time, to the extent and on the terms it thinks fit`
        IF (`ground (i)` OR `the court is satisfied the delay came from the defendant and was reasonable`) AND `the court is satisfied it is just`
        THEN `the court may extend the time, to the extent and on the terms it thinks fit`
        OTHERWISE `this section gives no extension on these facts`
    WHERE
        `the year before the last day` MEANS `the anniversary` (-1) `years after` `the last day`
        `the year after learning` MEANS `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day I learnt them`
        `ground (i)` MEANS
            `material facts were learnt late`
                AND `the court is satisfied the facts are material`
                AND (`the day I learnt them` `is after` `the year before the last day`)
                AND (NOT (`the day I instituted or will institute` `is after` `the year after learning`))

§§ `s 44A -- the court's power to extend for defamation`

-- s 44A(2): "The court may extend the limitation period to a period of up to 3 years running from the date of the
-- alleged publication of the matter if the plaintiff satisfies the court that it is just and reasonable to allow an action
-- to proceed." (3): "may not order the extension ... other than in the circumstances specified in subsection (2)."
-- s 44C: even after the period has expired.
DECLARE `Defamation extension` IS ONE OF
    `the court may extend it up to` HAS `the extended last day` IS A DATE
    `the court may not extend it`

GIVEN `the publication day` IS A DATE
      `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Defamation extension`
`s 44A -- the defamation extension` `the publication day` `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable`
    THEN `the court may extend it up to` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the publication day`)
    ELSE `the court may not extend it`

§§ `s 24 -- contribution between tortfeasors`

-- s 24(1): "not maintainable if brought after the first to expire of: (a) a limitation period of 2 years from the date on
-- which the right of action to recover contribution first accrued ...; or (b) a limitation period of 4 years from the date
-- of the expiration of the limitation period for the principal action." (2): it accrues on the day of the judgment or
-- award fixing the liability, or else of the agreement fixing its amount. (3): the principal action's period under this
-- or any other enactment. Where the principal action has no limitation period (child abuse, dust disease), (b) never
-- expires and (a) alone applies (fork F7).
GIVEN `the day my liability was fixed` IS A DATE
      `the principal action has a limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal action's last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 24 -- the last day for contribution` `the day my liability was fixed` `the principal action has a limitation period` `the principal action's last day` MEANS
    IF `the principal action has a limitation period`
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the anniversary` 2 `years after` `the day my liability was fixed`) `and` (`the anniversary` 4 `years after` `the principal action's last day`)
    ELSE `the anniversary` 2 `years after` `the day my liability was fixed`

§§ `s 8 -- set-off and counterclaim`

-- s 8: "a claim by way of set-off or counter-claim shall be deemed to be a separate action and to have commenced on the
-- same date as the action in which the set-off or counter-claim is pleaded."
GIVEN `the day the action against me was commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 8 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `the day the action against me was commenced` MEANS `the day the action against me was commenced`

§§ `s 48A -- amending after the period has expired`

-- s 48A(1): "If a court would, but for the expiry of a relevant period of limitation after the day a proceeding in the
-- court has commenced, allow a party to amend a document in the proceeding, the court shall allow the amendment to be made
-- if it is satisfied that no other party ... would by reason of the amendment be prejudiced ... in a way that could not be
-- met by an adjournment, an award of costs or otherwise." (2): "does not apply to an amendment in a proceeding commenced
-- before the commencement of this section" (1 November 1987): JUST FALSE. The court not satisfied, or the amendment not
-- otherwise allowable: the section is silent (NOTHING-kind: silent).
GIVEN `the day the proceeding commenced` IS A DATE
      `the court would otherwise allow it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied no other party is prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A -- the court must allow my amendment` `the day the proceeding commenced` `the court would otherwise allow it` `the court is satisfied no other party is prejudiced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the proceeding commenced` `is before` `the section 48A commencement day`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the court would otherwise allow it` AND `the court is satisfied no other party is prejudiced`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part V Division 2 -- child abuse claims decided before 15 June 2017 (ss 53-55)`

DECLARE `Earlier outcome` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: no earlier action, judgment or settlement`
    `a judgment that the limitation period had expired`
    `a judgment for legal professional negligence on the ground that the period had expired`
    `a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds`
    `a settlement made because the claim was out of time`
    `a settlement made for other reasons`
    `an action started before 15 June 2017 and still undecided then`

DECLARE `Where Part V leaves my claim` IS ONE OF
    `I may sue: section 5A applies directly`
    `I may sue despite the earlier judgment or settlement, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
    `I cannot sue again: a court finally decided the matter on other grounds`
    `section 5A applies to my pending action`
    `the Act does not clearly say`
    `not a child abuse action`

-- s 54(1): "An action may be brought after the commencement on a cause of action even if, before the commencement, a
-- judgment on the cause of action has been given on the ground that a limitation period applying to the cause of action
-- had expired." (2): the same for a judgment "in respect of legal professional negligence". (3): "However, an action
-- cannot be brought ... where, before the commencement, a court had given judgment in final determination of a matter on
-- grounds other than that a limitation period ... had expired." (4): "as if the action in which the previous judgment was
-- given had not itself been commenced." s 53(2): a "judgment given" "extends to an agreement entered into in relation to
-- settlement" of child abuse damages. s 55: an action brought before the commencement with no judgment at the
-- commencement: "Section 5A applies ... to remove the previously applying limitation period."
-- s 54 is read with its Division as reaching child abuse claims only (finding 7); a settlement made for other reasons is
-- not "given on the ground" that the period had expired, and s 54(3) speaks only of "a court" (NOTHING-kind: silent,
-- finding 8).
GIVEN `it is a child abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what happened before 15 June 2017` IS A `Earlier outcome`
GIVETH A `Where Part V leaves my claim`
`ss 53-55 -- where Part V leaves my claim` `it is a child abuse action` `what happened before 15 June 2017` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is a child abuse action`
    THEN `not a child abuse action`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened before 15 June 2017`
         WHEN `nothing: no earlier action, judgment or settlement` THEN `I may sue: section 5A applies directly`
         WHEN `a judgment that the limitation period had expired` THEN `I may sue despite the earlier judgment or settlement, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
         WHEN `a judgment for legal professional negligence on the ground that the period had expired` THEN `I may sue despite the earlier judgment or settlement, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
         WHEN `a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds` THEN `I cannot sue again: a court finally decided the matter on other grounds`
         WHEN `a settlement made because the claim was out of time` THEN `I may sue despite the earlier judgment or settlement, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
         WHEN `a settlement made for other reasons` THEN `the Act does not clearly say`
         WHEN `an action started before 15 June 2017 and still undecided then` THEN `section 5A applies to my pending action`

-- s 54(5): "the court hearing the action may, if it considers it is just and reasonable to do so, ... (a) set aside any
-- judgment as mentioned in subsection (1) or (2)". (6): "The Supreme Court may, on application, exercise the power ...
-- even though it is not hearing the action." (7): "A court (other than the Supreme Court) may not exercise the power ...
-- to set aside a judgment of any other court." The "if" and "may not" give JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `it is the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is hearing my action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment is that court's own` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54(5)-(7) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `it is the Supreme Court` `it is hearing my action` `the judgment is that court's own` `the court considers it just and reasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court considers it just and reasonable`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `it is the Supreme Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the judgment is that court's own`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `it is hearing my action`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
